				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/imthatoneguyirl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3987471); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3987471&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606100941" alt="ImThatOneGuyIRL" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3987471)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/imthatoneguyirl" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3987471); return false;" >ImThatOneGuyIRL</a></span> <span class="odate time_1562599827 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Jul 2019 15:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4301214">
									

<p>The images, voice recordings, and format in general were very well created for this scip. I also love the idea of the scip itself; an influence that controls its victims to the point where even the researchers assigned to the scip question their sanity.</p>
<p>Just a few minor formatting errors and typoes:</p>
<p>&quot;The dexterity of the SCP-4965-1's movement&quot;<br />
Describing the anomalies as &quot;instances of SCP-4965-1&quot; rather than &quot;SCP-4965-1s&quot; fits more into SCP document syntax.</p>
<p>In one of the logs, the question &quot;How have you been effecting the monitoring equipment and security systems&quot; is asked.<br />
The &quot;effecting&quot; should be replaced with &quot;affecting&quot;.</p>
<p>In the special containment procedures, you write &quot;All residents are screened for SCP-4965 and all infected humans become designated as SCP-4965-1&quot;.<br />
This sentence feels moderately repetitive. Maybe seperate it into two sentences and describe the effect the SCP has on its hosts? And remember, the hosts are instances of SCP-4965-1 before they are identified. They aren't instances only after being found, which the sentence confusingly suggests.<br />
If you want to keep this part in one sentence, I'd suggest using something like &quot;All residents are screened and examined for characteristics of SCP-4965-1. SCP-4965-1 is the term used for instances&#8230;&quot; and so on and so forth.</p>
<p>Overall, good job! I look forward to seeing more scips written by you in the near future.</p>

							</div>

								
					
